# shadcn/ui

This repo is already configured via `components.json` (style: **base-vega**, Base UI, RSC, aliases under `@/components` and `@/lib/utils`).

## Prefer shadcn primitives

When you need a common UI primitive, **use shadcn — do not build a custom equivalent**.

Examples: dropdown/menu, dialog, sheet, popover, select, tabs, accordion, tooltip, checkbox, switch, radio, slider, toast/sonner.

1. Check whether the component already exists in `src/components/ui/`.
2. If it does not, add it with the CLI (do not hand-roll the primitive):

```bash
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>
```

3. Build domain UI (header, sections, pages) **on top of** those primitives in `src/components/`.

### Do / don't

```tsx
// DON'T — custom dropdown / focus / dismiss logic
const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
return <button onClick={() => setOpen(true)}>...</button>;

// DO — shadcn primitive
import {
  DropdownMenu,
  DropdownMenuContent,
  DropdownMenuItem,
  DropdownMenuTrigger,
} from '@/components/ui/dropdown-menu';
```

Only skip shadcn when there is no matching primitive, or an existing domain pattern in the repo already covers the need.

## Conventions

- shadcn primitives belong in `src/components/ui/`.
- Domain components live in `src/components/` (and feature folders such as `header/`).
- Prefer extending existing `ui/` components and domain patterns rather than duplicating primitives.
